WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:01.253
(uptempo music)

00:00:01.253 --> 00:00:02.434
- [Narrator] You probably remember this

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.824
hilarious moment from
When Harry Met Sally.

00:00:04.824 --> 00:00:08.103
- Then she tells you her stories,
you tell her your stories.

00:00:08.103 --> 00:00:10.049
- [Narrator] Well, this
ridiculous rom-com scene

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:13.602
is indicative of a real and
very serious sport, which,

00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:17.769
believe it or not, introduced
society to sport betting.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.533
Competitive walking, better know to some

00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:26.695
as pedestrianism, started in the 1800s.

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:28.666
Aristocrats at that time had footmen

00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:30.283
whose job was to carry messages

00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.425
from one aristocrat to another.

00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:34.576
It was only a matter of
time until the aristocrats

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:37.337
started making wagers on
whose footman was faster.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.305
Thus, the birth of sport
betting as we know it.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.364
(cheering)
(dramatic music)

00:00:41.364 --> 00:00:43.884
Competitive walking grew
into a real sporting event,

00:00:43.884 --> 00:00:47.071
and reached its peak
in the 1870s and 1880s,

00:00:47.071 --> 00:00:48.344
when spectators would show up in

00:00:48.344 --> 00:00:51.559
Super Bowl-like masses to see
people walk competitively.

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:54.396
They even filled up the
original Madison Square Garden.

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:55.229
Wow.

00:00:55.229 --> 00:00:57.746
Sometimes races would last up to six days

00:00:57.746 --> 00:01:00.442
and the atmosphere was
almost festival-like.

00:01:00.442 --> 00:01:02.958
Brass bands played,
vendors sold pickled eggs,

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:04.919
maybe even some roasted chestnuts.

00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:06.169
Yum.

00:01:06.169 --> 00:01:07.876
The competitions drew everyone,

00:01:07.876 --> 00:01:10.617
from celebrities to
politicians, even regular folk.

00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:11.744
Champagne, of all things, was

00:01:11.744 --> 00:01:13.353
the drink of choice for walkers.

00:01:13.353 --> 00:01:14.677
They thought it was a stimulant,

00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:17.083
and, as one would, they
drank it by the bottle.

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:18.700
And, guess what, it kinda worked.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.526
One guy walked 136 miles in just 34 hours.

00:01:22.526 --> 00:01:23.443
Bottoms up.

